    add();add('| Bank | Observed-zero source offsets | Retained source F offsets | Source native minimum margin | Source temperature unit | False / missed target F pairs | Source fit seconds |')
    add('|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|')
    for r in s['source_banks']:add(f"| {r['bank']} | {r['zero_offsets']} | {r['source_retained_offsets']} | {r['native_source_delta']:.6f} | {r['unit']:.9f} | {r['target_false_forbidden_pairs']} / {r['target_missed_forbidden_pairs']} | {r['fit_seconds']:.6f} |")
    add();add('All banks infer the same four primitive lines and use 224 grouped couplings plus one shared unary. Source counts, marginals, exposure, lines and grouping are recomputed from each bank. F retains zero-count finite offsets whose marginal exposure is at least ln(264/0.01), together with the inferred lines. The positive-F derivative keeps learned positive coefficients on that support, sets unary/off-support weights to zero, extends lines to N13 and gives newly representable off-line offsets zero weight. Its temperature unit is the float32 mean coefficient across unique retained canonical **source** offsets. This derivative is distinct from the native soft BP AdamW energy.')
    add();add('Each fit uses zero initialization, 4,000 AdamW updates, learning rate 0.3 with the original cosine denominator 4,000, decay 0.01, betas (0.9,0.999), epsilon 1e-8, float32, TF32 disabled and no preconditioner. The hash-pinned H3u PL function exactly aggregates all 298 one/two/three-clue subsets per source board: occupied free-cell multiplicity 231 and empty-cell multiplicity 298. All four fits pass finite-parameter, positive native-margin, positive retained-weight and transferred-edge gates. Literal expanded-clue losses/gradients and actual-bank CPU/GPU gradients were checked before fitting; all source counts, exposure, grouping and transferred weights were independently reconstructed.')
    add();add('For each bank, source calibration embeds its N12 source boards into N13 coordinates and samples 4,096 unique clue inputs: 2 one-clue, 205 two-clue and 3,889 three-clue inputs, with seeds 2026112710–2026112713. Calibration opens no target data arrays, keys or labels and computes no target accuracy. Its integrity guard checks source files and source-only historical validation receipts; target artifact hashes are checked only in the later target phase. Every new calibration key, including overlaps and any failed-bank keys, enters the target exclusion union.')
    add();add('The reference cap is 20,000 arbitrary proposals; the fixed permutation grid is 8,000/12,000/16,000. Each configuration runs source streams 101/102/103 on both physical GPUs, with reversed configuration order by GPU and stream parity. Selection minimizes absolute relative median-time error, ties favoring the smaller cap. The protocol permits one deterministic interpolation, rounded to a multiple of 128, only if the fixed grid misses ±5%; it forbids extrapolation or further adjustment. Each chosen cap and full timing receipt is sealed before any common fresh target is reserved.')
    add();add('| Bank | Selected permutation cap | Source arbitrary / permutation median seconds | Source ratio | Source ratio 5th/95th bootstrap endpoints | Interpolation |')
    add('|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|')
    for b in banks:
        c=s['calibration_selections'][str(b['bank'])];g=c['all_calibration_groups'];a=g['arbitrary-c20000']['median_seconds'];z=g[f"permutation-c{c['selected_permutation_cap']}"]['median_seconds'];lo,hi=c['source_ratio_seed_cluster_bootstrap_5_95'];add(f"| {b['bank']} | {c['selected_permutation_cap']:,} | {a:.6f} / {z:.6f} | {c['source_median_time_ratio']:.6f} | {lo:.6f} / {hi:.6f} | {c['interpolation_used']} |")
    add();add('The source matching gate is a point-median gate, separate from its uncertainty. The source bootstrap resamples three streams while retaining both devices per stream; six timings are not six independent learning or search draws. All individual source timings, proposals and acceptances are retained in the tracked calibration export. The schedule is T(k)=u·0.01^(k/(cap−1)); varying the cap changes annealing duration while keeping bank-specific endpoints fixed. Thus this compares declared matched-compute recipes, not proposal type at an identical proposal-index schedule.')
    add();add(f"The fresh target cohort uses seed **2026112516**, excludes **{d['prior_search_and_calibration_keys']:,}** historical search/calibration keys plus the union of **{d['new_unique_calibration_keys']:,}** new calibration keys, and draws from **{d['eligible_keys']:,}** remaining inputs. The exclusion union has {d['all_excluded_keys']:,} distinct keys. The cohort has {d['by_clues']['1']} / {d['by_clues']['2']} / {d['by_clues']['3']} one/two/three-clue inputs, {d['compatible_completions']:,} compatible completions, and zero overlap with the exclusion union. Data SHA: `{d['data_sha256']}`.")
    add();add('Every bank and method receives the same complete saved permutation initialization for each input/chain/search seed. The initializer uses a separate CPU stream; GPU proposal generators are reset separately. There are 20 chains and seeds 0/1/2. Physical-device crossover is preserved for every bank. The strict certificate is an exact integer zero count of occupied F edges, including given–given pairs, with q=13 preserved. Independently valid stopped outputs define the abstaining primary. Certificate-first energy fallback and distinct-solution coverage remain secondary.')
    add();add('| Bank | Inputs with valid zero-F completion / 4,096 | Certified ceiling (%) | Compatible zero-F / all completions | Complete zero-F / 1,932 target solutions | Given-given F conflicts |')
